# TypeORM Migrations — Standards

> **DDL only. No DML in migrations unless absolutely necessary.**

---

## 📝 Migration Naming

Format: `{timestamp}-{Description}.ts`

```
1770300000000-AddCustomerStatusColumn.ts
1770400000000-CreateSiteVisitTable.ts
```

---

## 🏗️ Migration Template

```typescript
import { MigrationInterface, QueryRunner } from 'typeorm';

export class AddCustomerStatusColumn1770300000000 implements MigrationInterface {
  name = 'AddCustomerStatusColumn1770300000000';

  public async up(queryRunner: QueryRunner): Promise<void> {
    // DDL operations only
    await queryRunner.query(`
      ALTER TABLE "customer_profiles"
      ADD COLUMN "status" varchar(20) DEFAULT 'active'
    `);
  }

  public async down(queryRunner: QueryRunner): Promise<void> {
    await queryRunner.query(`
      ALTER TABLE "customer_profiles"
      DROP COLUMN "status"
    `);
  }
}
```

---

## 🎯 Patterns

**Adding column:**
```sql
ALTER TABLE "table_name" ADD COLUMN "column_name" type DEFAULT value;
```

**Creating table:**
```sql
CREATE TABLE "table_name" (
  "id" uuid PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT uuid_generate_v4(),
  "created_at" timestamptz DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,
  "updated_at" timestamptz DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,
  "deleted_at" timestamptz,
  -- other columns
);
```

**Adding index:**
```sql
CREATE INDEX "idx_table_column" ON "table_name" ("column_name")
WHERE deleted_at IS NULL;
```

**Auto-update trigger for updated_at:**
```sql
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION update_updated_at_column()
RETURNS TRIGGER AS $$
BEGIN
  NEW.updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
  RETURN NEW;
END;
$$ language 'plpgsql';

CREATE TRIGGER update_table_updated_at
  BEFORE UPDATE ON "table_name"
  FOR EACH ROW EXECUTE FUNCTION update_updated_at_column();
```

---

## 🚫 NEVER DO

❌ DML (INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE) in migrations  
❌ Drop columns/tables without down() migration  
❌ Modify existing migration files  
❌ Skip creating down() method  
❌ Hardcode data — use seeds for data

---

## ✅ ALWAYS DO

✓ Test migration up AND down locally  
✓ Add indexes for frequently queried columns  
✓ Include partial indexes for soft-deleted tables  
✓ Create triggers for `updated_at` timestamp fields
